        "text": {
          "en": "The Supreme People's Court of the People's Republic of China\nAnnouncement\nThe Reply of the Supreme People's Court on the Jurisdiction over Disputes concerning Liability for Damage Caused by an Application for Property Preservation in Litigation was adopted at the 1,722nd meeting of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court on 17 July 2017, is hereby promulgated and shall come into force on 10 August 2017.\n1 August 2017\nThe Supreme People's Court\nReply on the Jurisdiction over Disputes concerning Liability for Damage\nCaused by an Application for Property Preservation in Litigation\nFa Shi No. 14 [2017]\nThe Higher People's Court of Zhejiang Province:\nYour court's Request for Instructions on the Jurisdiction over Disputes concerning Liability for Damage Caused by an Application for Property Preservation in Litigation (Zhe Li Ta Zi No. 91 [2015]) has been received. After study, the following reply is given:\nIn order to facilitate litigation by the parties, an action for a dispute over liability for damage caused by an application for property preservation in litigation, instituted by the respondent or an interested party to the property preservation in litigation in accordance with Article 105 of the Civil Procedure Law of the People's Republic of China, shall be under the jurisdiction of the people's court that made the ruling on property preservation in litigation.\nThis is our reply."
        },
